   110	
   111	| Product | Admitted reads | Admitted changes | P09 treatment |
   112	|---|---|---|---|
   113	| AI Runtime Security | `ManagementResource` (profiles, topics, applications, API keys, deployment profiles, DLP catalog/profiles/patterns, filtering profiles, dictionaries, sessions); scan (`scan.rs`) | `ChangeKind` Profiles, Topics, Applications, ApiKeys, DataPatterns, DataProfiles, FilteringProfiles, Dictionaries with `ChangeAction` Create/Version/Rotate/Delete/… (`changes.rs`) | Full: Administration tabs, reviews, Playground, Inbox items |
   114	| AI Gateway | `GatewayRead` (inventory, detail, integration models, prerequisites, observe, MCP servers) | Gateway `ChangeKind`s (workspaces, providers, routes, guardrails, service/user keys, integrations) | Full, inside Administration; Harness lifecycle 2 reads `McpServers` |
   115	| AI Red Teaming | `red_team.rs` reads (scan inventory, statistics, static reports; C13) | none (execution stays a disabled preview) | Read-only card and tabs; Test Cases "Inspect" only |
   116	| Model/skill observability (AI Supply Chain in the prototype) | C13 model/skill reads | none | Read-only; shown under its C13 name, never as a scanning product |
   117	| Agentic Identity Security | none | none | **Not available in this release**: card and accordion entry with the dependency gate ("needs an admitted AIS service; see D058"); not selectable in the wizard; never verified; no inventory, no policy review |
   118	| Agentic Endpoint Security | none | none | Same as AIS; the prototype's AES policy review, discovered-AI table and warning demo are fixtures only and are not implemented |
   119	
   120	Rules: an unavailable product never produces a verification result, an
   121	Inbox item, an inventory row or a review. The wizard's verify step lists it
   122	as "Not available" (not pass, warning or fail). Test V2-T19 asserts that the
   123	admin inventory for an unavailable product has no tabs and no actions, and
   124	V2-R10 asserts that no intent exists that would mutate it.
   125	
   126	## 7. Error presentation
   127	
   128	- **Refusal** (core refused an intent): warn toast with the refusal reason and
   129	  the tenant named; never a modal. Guard-type refusals (tenant switch with a
   130	  pending decision) render their dialog from the refusal payload.
   131	- **Delivery unknown**: inline "not confirmed" state on the control that
   132	  dispatched, with Retry; the control is not reset.
   133	- **Contract violation**: generic warn toast; detail to diagnostics.
   134	
   135	## 8. Accessibility additions
   136	
   137	The native acceptance checklist gains four items that every P09 chunk's
   138	acceptance script asserts: accent-colour focus ring on every focusable
   139	control (inset variant where declared); `role="status"` live regions for read
   140	status, API send completion and review apply; one topmost modal with
   141	`aria-hidden` siblings and focus return; toasts persist under Reduce Motion.
